I had a spooky installation following your Github page. I installed "rexpokit", "cladoRcpp", "devtools", and finally "BioGeoBEARS" (from Github). I then tried to test if the installation worked following the script from one of my advisor's papers on Salvia (doi:10.1002/ajb2.1268), and IT DIDN'T WORK. BioGeoBEARS wasn't installed at all in R. It was only after installing the following packages from the previous script (see below) that I was able to get BioGeoBEARS installed correctly. Later, I ran into the following error:

Error in bears_optim_run(BioGeoBEARS_run_object) :
  lazy-load database '/Library/Frameworks/R.framework/Versions/4.3-x86_64/Resources/library/cladoRcpp/R/cladoRcpp.rdb' is corrupt

I solved it by removing "cladoRcpp" from my library, as suggested by Nick's Github for "BioGeoBEARS". This solution finally made it work!

Additional packages installed suggested from Salvia script
#install.packages("parallel")
library(parallel)
#install.packages("optimx", dependencies=TRUE, repos="http://cran.rstudio.com")
library(optimx)
#install.packages("snow")
library(snow)
#install.packages("phylobase", dependencies=TRUE, repos="http://cran.rstudio.com")
library(phylobase)
#install.packages("ape")
library(ape)

Happy Day of the Dead! I hope CRAN won't add new dead packages to this day...

nicole

